Modifications:

- substantially adapted the public typed event, message, and properties
  contract into a best-effort-only Proctor message type with validation,
  cloning, and hard data/property bounds (no durable/reliable send class);
- retained the one-handler-per-event, broadcast, targeted-send, and explicit
  start/stop concepts from Mattermost's public cluster boundary;
- omitted enterprise-only discovery, gossip, leader election, transport,
  support-packet, log-query, plugin-status, and cross-node WebSocket queue
  implementations; no commercial or enterprise cluster source was copied;
- implemented an original Proctor local transport as the single-node
  degenerate architecture, with peer-only no-op broadcasts and explicit
  self-targeted handler dispatch;
- implemented an original Proctor Memberlist multi-node transport with
  encrypted gossip, PostgreSQL discovery leases for bootstrap seeds, and
  best-effort direct peer messaging (no Redis service required for
  clustering; Redis remains optional only as disposable cache);
- substantially adapted Mattermost's CPU-sharded node-owned hub, bounded
  send/dead queue, per-connection sequencing, ping/pong, reconnect/replay,
  backpressure, and WebSocket router concepts for Proctor's Gorilla HTTP
  boundary and immutable principals;
- replaced Mattermost channel/team filters and session role snapshots with
  explicit Proctor action/resource subscriptions authorized through the same
  current-state, durably audited application authorization service as HTTP;
- retained Mattermost's local-first publication followed by a cluster publish
  whose peer handler performs local-only delivery, preventing rebroadcast
  loops;
- added best-effort cross-node session revocation, access-cache invalidation,
  and permission-change connection invalidation, with correctness recovering
  from PostgreSQL and bounded cache TTLs when messages are lost;
- made platform startup gate server readiness and made platform shutdown own
  transport cleanup, while draining WebSocket connections before stopping the
